<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Abecafe to conduct survey on coffee crop.</title>
<headline>Brazil Abecafe to conduct survey on coffee crop.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian Coffee Exporters' Association (Abecafe) is to conduct a survey of members on prospects for the 1997/98 Brazilian crop and hopes to have a forecast ready on Feb 19, Abecafe's president said.</p>
<p>&quot;We think around 30 of the 45 members will participate,&quot; said Jorge Esteve.</p>
<p>Brazilian Coffee Exporters' Federation is the traditional exporters' group but in 1994 by a group of exporters formed Abecafe, principally because they opposed a private sector plan dividing out coffee exports internally.</p>
<p>Companies within Abecafe include Cargill Agricola, Esteve Irmaos, Volcafe and Rio Doce Cafe. According to the association, members accounted for 47 percent of Brazil exports in 1996.</p>
<p>--Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
